## Task Tracking
- Tasks live in `tasks.json` (manage with `ch tasks`). Optional markdown export: `ch tasks export --md`.

## Known Issues
- **Apostrophe in project path:** The path "Claude's Home" contains an apostrophe which can cause glob/search failures in subagents. When delegating file searches to subagents, ensure paths are properly quoted or escaped.

See `memory/` for detailed profiles and context.

## CLI Tools (ch) — prefer over Read/Edit for tasks & memory

Install once: `cd cli && npm link`. Then use `ch ...` from anywhere, or `./ch ...` from repo root.

| Operation | Command |
|-----------|---------|
| Dump active tasks (JSON) | `ch tasks dump --active` |
| Add a task | `ch tasks add "<title>" [--section todo] [--priority medium] [--due YYYY-MM-DD] [--estimate 2h] [--assignee name] [--label L] [--blocked]` |
| Move task to section | `ch tasks move <id> <section>` |
| Mark done | `ch tasks done <id>` (refuses open subtasks: `--force`, or `update <id> --promote-subtask N`; closes the epic when it was its last open child) |
| Ship to review | `ch tasks review <id> --shipped "..." --check "..."` (needs a `--check`, or `--no-checks "<reason>"`; `--check-project N=<path>` / `--check-video N=<path>` / `--check-audio N=<path>` attach a saved .agsproj / short .mp4 / .wav under `$CH_HOME/evidence` to the Nth `--check`; `--check-no-video N=<reason>` says why that check has no video (not together with `--check-video`); to add or replace evidence on an existing check later: `ch tasks update <id> --check-video N=<path>` (also `--check-project`/`--check-audio`/`--check-no-video`, N as `ch tasks get` lists it); `--resolve-unverified N` / `--clear-unverified` drop Unverified lines; a `ui`/`audio` ticket needs `--evidence <path>` or `--unverified` lines tagged `taste:` / `hardware:` / `outside:` / `consent:`, `--force "<why>"` overrides; an open PR link refuses the review unless `--held-pr "<why>"` (held open on purpose: adds the check "Try on branch X, then say merge or not"); a review that would leave its open epic with only backlog tickets is refused: move them to a "(later)" epic or todo, or `--allow-parked "<why>"`); `--ask "<question>"` (repeatable) leaves a question for Tal |
| Ask Tal to decide | `ch tasks ask <id> "<question, max 140 chars>" --option "A: ..." --option "B: ..." [--recommend A] [--details "..."] [--video\|--audio\|--image\|--project <path under evidence/>] [--same-as <id>] [--merge-pr URL]` (sets waitingOn; shows in the Plan page's For you list while the ticket or its epic is open, with option buttons and Park). Only choices are asks: a taste question is a check, `--unverified "needs-tal: taste: <what> \| video=<path>"` on `ch tasks review` (refused without media). List: `ch tasks asks [--refresh]`; resolve: `ch tasks answer <id> [<key>] <A\|B\|"reply">` / `--done` / `--dismiss` / `--park "<why>"` (records the decision and clears waitingOn; on a done ticket it files a follow-up) |
| Update fields | `ch tasks update <id> --title "..." --description "..." --priority high --due ... --estimate 30m --assignee ...` |
| Add a note (with screenshots) / edit one | `ch tasks update <id> --add-note "..." [--note-image file.png]...` / `--edit-note N --note-text "..."`; `ch tasks get <id>` prints `image: <path>` per image: open it with the Read tool |
| Record an agent run of a check | `ch tasks update <id> --verify-check N --verify-note "<how it was run>" [--verify-result pass\|fail] [--verify-by name]` (note 10+ chars; never ticks the check, the tick stays Tal's; `--unverify-check N` removes the marker; shown on the Plan page as "Agent verified <date>" or "Agent: failed") |
| List checks no agent has run | `ch tasks checks [--json]` (unticked, not handed-off, unverified checks on open epics and in-progress/review tickets, as `<id>#<n> <text>`) |
| Next available id | `ch tasks next-id` |
| Validate tasks.json | `ch tasks lint [--fix]` |
| Markdown snapshot | `ch tasks export --md` |
| Person fields | `ch mem person <slug> [--field slack_id,email] [--json]` |
| Fuzzy person lookup | `ch mem whois "<name>"` |
| Memory index (JSON) | `ch mem index --json` |
| Session digest | `ch context [--json]` |
| List pending gaps | `ch gaps list` |
| Resolve a gap | `ch gaps resolve <n>` |
| Recent Slack activity (JSON) | `ch slack recent --days <N> --user <UID>` |
| Channel activity (JSON) | `ch slack channels --ids <C1,C2> --days <N>` |
| Read a thread | `ch slack thread --channel <C> --ts <ts>` |
| Check reactions | `ch slack reactions --channel <C> --ts <ts> [--user <U>]` |

ch slack reads its token (priority: SLACK_TOKEN env -> config.json slack_token_cmd, a command that prints the token to stdout, resolved at runtime -> config.json slack_token literal); outputs JSON; zero LLM tokens. `recent` needs an xoxp- USER token (search:read).

**Rules:**
- NEVER read `tasks.json` or `TASKS.md` directly — always use `ch tasks`.
- NEVER `ls memory/people` to check existence — use `ch mem person exists <slug>` or `ch mem whois`.
- `ch` enforces unique ids — do not guess the next id; call `ch tasks next-id`.
- If `CH_HOME` is unset, the CLI walks up from cwd to find the repo root automatically.

## Dashboard
- **Run with:** `node serve.js` (from project root) — opens at `http://localhost:3000/dashboard/`
- Dashboard-specific conventions live in `dashboard/CLAUDE.md` — copy `dashboard/CLAUDE.md.example` to create it. It loads only when working under `dashboard/`, keeping it out of every other session.
